    20→
    21→/// Body request implemented as a [Future].
    22→///
    23→/// The future will poll the underlying request until fulfilled.
    24→/// If the response arrived with insufficient number of bodies, the future
    25→/// will issue another request until all bodies are collected.
    26→///
    27→/// It then proceeds to verify the downloaded bodies. In case of a validation error,
    28→/// the future will start over.
    29→///
    30→/// The future will filter out any empty headers (see [`alloy_consensus::Header::is_empty`]) from
    31→/// the request. If [`BodiesRequestFuture`] was initialized with all empty headers, no request will
    32→/// be dispatched and they will be immediately returned upon polling.
    33→///
    34→/// NB: This assumes that peers respond with bodies in the order that they were requested.
    35→/// This is a reasonable assumption to make as that's [what Geth
    36→/// does](https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/blob/f53ff0ff4a68ffc56004ab1d5cc244bcb64d3277/les/server_requests.go#L245).
    37→/// All errors regarding the response cause the peer to get penalized, meaning that adversaries
    38→/// that try to give us bodies that do not match the requested order are going to be penalized
    39→/// and eventually disconnected.
    40→pub(crate) struct BodiesRequestFuture<B: Block, C: BodiesClient<Body = B::Body>> {
    41→    client: Arc<C>,
    42→    consensus: Arc<dyn Consensus<B, Error = ConsensusError>>,
    43→    metrics: BodyDownloaderMetrics,
    44→    /// Metrics for individual responses. This can be used to observe how the size (in bytes) of
    45→    /// responses change while bodies are being downloaded.
    46→    response_metrics: ResponseMetrics,
    47→    // Headers to download. The collection is shrunk as responses are buffered.
    48→    pending_headers: VecDeque<SealedHeader<B::Header>>,
    49→    /// Internal buffer for all blocks
    50→    buffer: Vec<BlockResponse<B>>,
    51→    fut: Option<C::Output>,
    52→    /// Tracks how many bodies we requested in the last request.
    53→    last_request_len: Option<usize>,
    54→}
    55→
    56→impl<B, C> BodiesRequestFuture<B, C>
